# Finance UI Concepts v1

## Design Principles

| # | Principle | Implication for later UI |
| - | --------- | ------------------------ |
| D1 | **Case is the unit** | Surfaces organize around an interpreted commercial situation, not payment/receipt/ledger/registration tables as the primary model |
| D2 | **Interpretation chain is the interaction model** | Operator flow expresses `facts → verdict → owner → lane → confidence → allow/forbid` |
| D3 | **Verdict explains facts; never replaces them** | Facts remain visible; verdict is a reading, not a stored status |
| D4 | **Ownership before affordances** | Action offers appear only after “whose move” is clear |
| D5 | **Wait is success** | Calm waiting is a first-class outcome, not an empty-state failure |
| D6 | **Healthy coexistence is non-alarming** | Evidence in review + unsettled settlement can be expected |
| D7 | **Altitude discipline** | Daily / exception / audit are distinct modes; ledger is not daily workflow |
| D8 | **Capability vs binder** | Reusable concepts use universal vocabulary; Denali supplies copy, subject shape, and business context |
| D9 | **No SoT merge** | Lifecycle, payment/intent, proof, and settlement stay separate axes |
| D10 | **Signals ≠ Cases** | Queues may signal work; opening work always lands in Case interpretation |

**Multi-workspace marks:** **U** universal · **Ad** adapter/product · **D** Denali-only wording/example  

**Probes:** **A** enrollment + offline evidence · **B** subscription + recurring · **C** marketplace order  

---

## Case Information Hierarchy

Not organized around payments list, receipts list, ledger entries, or registrations table.

### Level 1 — Immediate understanding

What the operator must grasp **first** (Pattern Encounter + Verdict headline):

| Concept | Purpose | Mark |
| ------- | ------- | ---- |
| Subject identity | Who / what commercial thing | **U** (**Ad** fields) |
| Interpretive verdict (headline) | Where we are financially *as a reading* | **U** |
| Next-action owner | Whose move | **U** |
| Work lane | daily / exception / audit | **U** |
| Alarm flag | Whether coexistence is healthy | **U** |

### Level 2 — Facts that explain the interpretation

| Concept | Purpose | Mark |
| ------- | ------- | ---- |
| Lifecycle eligibility | May money proceed? | **U** (**Ad** mapping) |
| Collection policy | Money due or not | **U** (**Ad** modes) |
| Obligation / remaining | Money target | **U** |
| Evidence / proof progress | Ingress state | **U** (**Ad** file vs gateway) |
| Intent state | Open/captured intents (+ provenance when known) | **U** |
| Settlement meaning | Product projection unsettled/partial/settled | **U** |
| Partial scope (if partial) | Which layer is partial | **U** |

### Level 3 — Ownership decision revealed

| Concept | Purpose | Mark |
| ------- | ------- | ---- |
| Owner category | counterparty / finance / product_desk / policy_system / exception_policy / idle | **U** |
| Explicit non-ownership | “Not finance’s move — waiting on X” | **U** |
| Confidence: why mine / why visible | Confidence quartet (partial) | **U** |

### Level 4 — Allowed actions

| Concept | Purpose | Mark |
| ------- | ------- | ---- |
| Allowed action set | From CaseOutput, not from clicked row | **U** |
| Forbidden action set | What to avoid now | **U** |
| Primary posture | act now / wait / escalate / inspect | **U** |

### Level 5 — History / audit

| Concept | Purpose | Mark |
| ------- | ------- | ---- |
| Evidence history (accepted/rejected prior) | Context for retry | **U** |
| Intent history | Parallel/duplicate detection | **U** |
| Ledger / recon | Audit altitude only | **U** |
| Product lifecycle timeline | Eligibility context (**Ad**) | **Ad** |

**Rule:** Level 5 must not outrank Levels 1–4 in daily mode.

---

## Encounter Model

### Intent

Operator discovers work without being tricked into treating raw signals as the mental model.

### Signal vs Case

| Signal (intake cue) | Case (interpreted situation) |
| -------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Pending evidence | AWAITING_FINANCE (likely) — finance may own review |
| Unpaid / unsettled obligation | May be awaiting counterparty, not eligible, no money due, or in review — **must interpret** |
| Exception cue | EXCEPTION lane — not routine review |
| Audit / recon finding | AUDIT altitude — not daily first response |

**Signals may form queues.** Queues are **indexes of attention**, not the definition of work.

### Encounter contract

```text
Signal selected
  → resolve commercial subject
  → open Financial Case (interpretation frame)
  → run Understanding → Verdict → Ownership before actions
```

### Queue without becoming the model

| Allowed | Forbidden |
| ------- | --------- |
| “Evidence needing review” as a **signal list** that opens Cases | Treating a receipt row as the whole job |
| “Unsettled subjects” as a **signal list** that opens Cases | Treating unpaid badge as finance task assignment |
| Exception inbox as signals | Happy-path approve from the inbox without Case frame |

### Multi-workspace

| Probe | Encounter signals | Mark |
| ----- | ----------------- | ---- |
| A | Pending offline proofs; unsettled enrollments | **U** + **D** labels |
| B | Failed charges; past_due invoices; disputes | **U** + **Ad** |
| C | Unpaid orders; capture disputes; payout holds | **U** + **Ad** (multi-case risk) |

---

## Understanding Model

Conceptual reveal order (UI Concepts must preserve this sequence in interaction architecture):

### Identity

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **Why needed** | Anchor the case; prevent wrong-party action |
| **If hidden** | Entity thrash; mis-capture |
| **Owner of fact** | **Workspace adapter** (display) + commercial id from finance/host |

### Eligibility

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **Why needed** | Money blame only when path is open |
| **If hidden** | Chase before product acceptance; process closed subjects as daily |
| **Owner of fact** | **Workspace** lifecycle → mapped to `not_yet` / `eligible` / `closed` |

### Policy

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **Why needed** | Distinguish money_due vs no_money_due |
| **If hidden** | Chase free/zero; invent evidence tasks |
| **Owner of fact** | **Workspace** collection policy resolution |

### Money

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **Why needed** | Obligation/remaining for evidence judgment and partial scope |
| **If hidden** | Approve/reject without amount; wrong club answers |
| **Owner of fact** | **Finance** (obligation port + invoice recognition) |

### Evidence

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **Why needed** | Ingress progress; decides finance vs counterparty ownership |
| **If hidden** | Confusion between “no proof” and “in review” |
| **Owner of fact** | **Finance** proof/receipt (or gateway evidence **Ad**) |

### Settlement

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **Why needed** | Product projection answer; coexistence with evidence |
| **If hidden** | Cannot answer “is payment OK?”; post-decision distrust |
| **Owner of fact** | **Finance** via settlement projection port (host-backed) |

### Context

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **Why needed** | Prioritization / ops context (service window, period, fulfillment) |
| **If hidden** | Poor prioritization — not wrong settlement meaning |
| **Owner of fact** | **Workspace adapter** businessContext (**D** departure/tour) |

**Checkpoint:** Understanding is incomplete until Identity→…→Settlement can support Owner derivation.

---

## Verdict Model

### Intent

Show “where we are financially?” as an **interpretive reading** that explains visible facts.

### Conceptual verdict set (non-exhaustive)

| Verdict | Operator meaning |
| ------- | ---------------- |
| `AWAITING_COUNTERPARTY` | Eligible, money due, waiting on counterparty |
| `AWAITING_FINANCE` | Evidence with finance; review owed |
| `SETTLED_CAPTURED` | Settled after accepted capture/evidence |
| `NO_MONEY_DUE` | No chase; idle on money |
| `NOT_ELIGIBLE` | Money path not open yet |
| `CLOSED` | Subject closed for normal collection |
| `PARTIAL` | Incomplete — scope required |
| `INTENT_OPEN_NO_PROOF` | Open intent ≠ in-review evidence |
| `EXCEPTION` | Commercial meaning unclear |
| `AUDIT_SUSPECT` | Daily story failed |

### Interaction rules

1. Verdict **explains** facts — facts stay available at Level 2.  
2. Verdict **does not replace** lifecycle, intent, proof, or settlement SoTs.  
3. Verdict **must not** be designed as a stored DB status or editable “case state.”  
4. Verdict always pairs with narrative + alarm rules (especially coexistence).  

### Example: `AWAITING_FINANCE`

Must communicate: evidence exists · finance owns · unsettled may be **expected**.  
Must not communicate: payment broken · sync failure.

### Multi-workspace

Verdict vocabulary = **U**. Frequency of evidence-review vs gateway settle = **Ad**.

---

## Ownership Model

### Intent

Answer “Whose move is it?” **before** offering actions.

### Owners

| Owner | Meaning |
| ----- | ------- |
| `counterparty` | Pay / submit / correct (**D** member; **Ad** subscriber/buyer) |
| `finance` | Review/decide evidence or finance-owned cleanup |
| `product_desk` | Eligibility/lifecycle desk |
| `policy_system` | No-money / policy completion |
| `exception_policy` | Exception judgment |
| `idle` | No money action |

### Why ownership before actions

- Prevents “I’m in finance UI ⇒ everything unsettled is mine.”  
- Makes **wait** a coherent choice when owner ≠ finance.  
- Aligns allow/forbid with who can legally/productively act.  

### Why actions without ownership confuse operators

Operators invent work (manual intent, ledger dive) or neglect real finance-owned evidence; club answers become inconsistent.

### Multi-workspace

Owner categories = **U**. Binding of counterparty/product_desk = **Ad**.

---

## Decision Model

### Intent

Action availability comes from interpretation output, not from which entity row was clicked.

### Source of truth for affordances

```text
CaseOutput.allowedActions
+ CaseOutput.forbiddenActions
(+ owner, lane, confidence)
```

**Not from:** clicked payment/receipt row · bare payment status · bare receipt status · ledger line.

### Conceptual postures

| Posture | When | Examples |
| ------- | ---- | -------- |
| **Act now** | owner=`finance`, lane=`daily`, allowed includes evidence decide | approve evidence, reject evidence |
| **Wait** | owner ∈ {counterparty, idle, product_desk, policy_system} | calm waiting (no irreversible finance act) |
| **Escalate** | lane=`exception` or allowed includes escalate | exception_policy handoff |
| **Inspect** | lane=`audit` or allowed includes inspect | audit context — after daily/exception fail |

### Rules

1. Irreversible acts require Understanding complete (hierarchy).  
2. Reject evidence returns ownership narrative to counterparty.  
3. Opening manual intent is **not** a default Decision posture (forbidden unless allowed for exception).  

### Multi-workspace

Postures = **U**. Which acts dominate = **Ad** (A: evidence review; B/C: more wait/inspect/dispute).

---

## Waiting Model

### Intent

Communicate: **Nothing is broken. Waiting is correct.**

### Calm waiting situations

| Situation | Message shape | Mark |
| --------- | ------------- | ---- |
| Awaiting counterparty (no evidence / rejected) | Waiting on counterparty — finance should not invent capture | **U** |
| Evidence in review + unsettled | Expected coexistence — finance acts (this is *not* calm-wait for finance; see coexistence) | **U** |
| No money due | No payment chase | **U** |
| Not eligible yet | Product desk owns eligibility | **U** |
| Idle settled | Case complete on money path | **U** |

**Note:** Healthy coexistence is **finance-owned work**, not calm waiting for finance — but it is **non-alarming** for settlement. Calm waiting applies when owner ≠ finance (or idle).

### Avoid alarm-based UX

- No error framing for expected waits  
- No forcing a primary destructive/create action to “resolve” waiting  
- Confidence: what happens if I do nothing = acceptable delay, not silent integrity loss  

### Multi-workspace

Calm waiting = **U**. Copy for counterparty action = **Ad/D**.

---

## Exception/Audit Model

### Exception (lane change)

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **When** | Terminal + leftover money objects; duplicate intents; non-healthy conflicts; policy disputes |
| **UI concept** | Visible mode change + reason trigger + routine approve/reject suppressed |
| **Owner** | typically `exception_policy` |
| **Mark** | **U** |

### Audit (altitude change)

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **When** | After daily/exception explanation fails, or recon finding |
| **Rules** | Never first response; not required for normal evidence approve; findings map back to Case Level 2 facts |
| **Mark** | **U** |

### Coexistence (daily, non-exception)

Evidence `in_review` + settlement `unsettled` → **not** exception by default → Verdict `AWAITING_FINANCE`, alarm=false (**U**, primary in **A**).

---

## Multi Workspace Compatibility

| UI Concept | A Enrollment+offline | B Subscription+recurring | C Marketplace order |
| ---------- | -------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------- |
| Case-first hierarchy | **U** | **U** | **U** (watch multi-case) |
| Signal queues ≠ Case model | **U** | **U** | **U** |
| Understanding order | **U** | **U** (**Ad** thin evidence) | **U** (**Ad** PSP) |
| Verdict-as-interpretation | **U** | **U** | **U** |
| Ownership before actions | **U** | **U** | **U** |
| Allow/forbid from CaseOutput | **U** | **U** | **U** |
| Calm waiting | **U** | **U** | **U** |
| Healthy coexistence | **U** (core path) | **Ad** if disputes | **Ad** if offline/dispute |
| Exception/audit modes | **U** | **U** | **U** |
| Tour/departure urgency | **D/Ad** | out | out |
| Member wording | **D** | **Ad** subscriber | **Ad** buyer |
| Offline proof approve as main act | **Ad** (central) | **Ad** (secondary) | **Ad** (secondary) |

**Survival rule:** If a concept requires tour, member, or offline-receipt to *define* the pattern (not merely bind copy), it fails multi-workspace and must be demoted to Denali binding.

---

## Denali Binding Notes

| Reusable concept | Denali binding |
| ---------------- | -------------- |
| commercialSubjectId | enrollment / registration id (no rename required in this phase) |
| subjectKind | enrollment |
| counterparty | member |
| product_desk | bookings / club ops |
| businessContext | tour title, departure proximity |
| collectionPolicy | offline evidence or free/zero from tour canonical |
| eligibility | booking lifecycle → not_yet / eligible / closed |
| evidence | offline transfer proof |
| settlementMeaning | booking paymentStatus projection |
| Signal queues | pending receipts; unpaid enrollments; bookings handoff |
| Local copy | club, tour, registration, member, “approve then offline pay” phrases |

Denali binding **may** use bookings APIs as **signals and fact sources**. It **must not** define the reusable IA as “bookings command center inside finance.”

---

## Implementation Deferred Decisions

| Deferred | Why deferred |
| -------- | ------------ |
| Visual layout, components, routes, navigation chrome | Explicitly out of this phase |
| Runtime `interpretFinancialCase` package | Optional for concepting; client composition rules acceptable until shared module |
| Renaming `registrationId` / settlement port | Conceptual alias only; no migration |
| Extensible collection-policy enum in APIs | Denali offline\|free sufficient for first binder |
| Subscription/marketplace ingress implementation | Need second product force |
| Persisting CaseOutput | Forbidden, not deferred |
| Replacing entity tabs wholesale in code | Implementation after UI Concepts acceptance + planning |

### Computation locus (accepted for next implementation planning)

For Denali-first delivery concepting: CaseOutput may be treated as **documented derivation** over existing fetches. A shared pure interpreter remains the **target** for multi-workspace consistency, not a gate to accept these UI Concepts.

---

## UI boundary

### Allowed (future implementation may build)

- Case frame expressing Levels 1–4  
- Signal queues that **open** Cases (not replace them)  
- Understanding reveal order  
- Interpretive verdict + narrative + ownership disclosure  
- Allow/forbid-driven postures: act / wait / escalate / inspect  
- Calm waiting and healthy coexistence messaging  
- Exception/audit mode changes  
- Denali bindings for copy, subject picker, urgency context  
- Client-side or shared derivation of CaseOutput from existing facts  

### Forbidden (recreates Denali lock-in or architecture breach)

- Payment/receipt/ledger/registration **as primary mental model**  
- Tour/departure as mandatory finance capability navigation  
- Member as universal counterparty in shared language  
- Offline receipt as sole payment flow in shared concepts  
- Booking lifecycle controls inside finance decision vocabulary  
- Persisted case status / merged status enum  
- Alarm UX for expected coexistence or calm waiting  
- Manual payment as default resolution of waiting  
- Ledger-first daily path  
- Cloning Denali tour IA for B/C  

### Deferred (needs runtime contracts or product force first)

- Shared interpreter package extract  
- SubjectKind multi-case platform rules in APIs  
- Gateway/recurring ingress UX beyond conceptual notes  
- Field renames / schema migrations  

---

## Concepts one-liner

> Finance operator UI Concepts organize around an interpreted Financial Case: signals only discover work; understanding reveals facts in order; verdict and ownership explain the situation; actions come from allow/forbid; waiting and coexistence stay calm; exception and audit are explicit altitudes — with Denali as the first binder, not the definition of finance UI.

---

*Conceptual UI architecture only. No screens, components, or implementation.*
